# A Worker does not inherit the document's CSP -- neither from a <meta> tag
# nor from a header on the document itself (MDN, CSP Web Workers API). The
# only way to give a worker a policy is a Content-Security-Policy response
# header on the worker script's own response. All file processing happens
# inside the worker, so without this rule the most sensitive part of the app
# runs with no CSP at all.
#
# Deliberately a single rule: Cloudflare Pages merges the headers of every
# matching rule and joins same-named headers with a comma, so a CSP on "/*"
# plus this one would hand the worker two concatenated policies.

/js/worker.js
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self';
